  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1227 PM CDT Thu Aug 13 2026\n\nAlthough slightly cooler, hot conditions are expected to continue \nthrough the weekend, becoming even hotter by early next week. The \nupper level ridge will continue to expand westward, amplifying over \nthe Plains regions into portions of the Intermountain west by early \nnext week. As a result, geopotential heights will remain stationary \njust around or slightly above seasonal averages as we see afternoon \nhighs in the upper 90s to lower triple digits. Becoming near heat \nadvisory level conditions by early to mid next week as the center of \nthe upper high sets up in the vicinity of the Caprock regions. As \nthe ridge expands westward, subsidence provided from the upper high \nwill likely limit overall precipitation chances while monsoonal \nmoisture remains confined to our west in portions of New Mexico. \nAlthough unlikely, we cannot rule out an isolated storm or two \ntracking into portions of the far southwestern Texas Panhandle both \nSaturday and Sunday afternoon and evenings. However, lack of \nmoisture and large scale ascent will likely hinder this from \nhappening.",
